          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "A useful implication is emerging: at a nondegenerate double zero, every auxiliary tilt’s first-order effect on the squared gap can be absorbed into a shift of collision time. A larger split therefore does not yet distinguish a useful flow. The distinction has to come from an estimate, controlled zero motion, or a measurable reduction in diagnostic cost."
            ]
